Overview

The Astrometric Simulation Engine (v1.2) is a hybrid astrophysics–plasma physics simulation framework integrating cosmic dataset ingestion, proton–laser interaction modeling, particle‑in‑cell (PIC) solvers, magnetohydrodynamic (MHD) coupling, GPU acceleration, and zero‑trust encryption.

The engine is designed to:

ingest astrophysical datasets (HDF5, FITS, GEANT4)

model proton–laser acceleration (TNSA, RPA)

simulate plasma dynamics using Vlasov–Maxwell PIC solvers

couple MHD fields to plasma evolution

operate securely under AES‑256/TLS 1.3 encryption

run on HPC clusters with GPU acceleration

This framework forms a secure, scalable, high‑energy simulation environment.

